WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.212
Unit 3 is the issuer
decision and the order.

2
00:00:03.212 --> 00:00:05.486
P K I and Certificates gives each class of

3
00:00:05.486 --> 00:00:08.150
certificate one issuer
and one renewal engine.

4
00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:13.032
Sequel server's T L S certificate comes
from the retained A D C S hierarchy,

5
00:00:13.032 --> 00:00:16.287
requested and renewed
through the C L M platform.

6
00:00:16.287 --> 00:00:22.025
Its deadline is the issuing C A it chains
to being retired, not A D C S as a whole.

7
00:00:22.025 --> 00:00:26.374
A certificate-mapped login or endpoint
isn't renewed by the platform,

8
00:00:26.374 --> 00:00:30.113
so it's replaced or re-mapped by
hand before its C A is retired.

9
00:00:30.113 --> 00:00:34.843
Domain controller certificates stay on
A D C S autoenrollment until the last

10
00:00:34.843 --> 00:00:39.425
domain controller retires, so the
interim posture keeps what it depends on.

11
00:00:39.425 --> 00:00:43.137
The kit turns each certificate's
use into a class and an action.

12
00:00:43.137 --> 00:00:46.912
It marks it yes when its issuer
is one of your enterprise C As,

13
00:00:46.912 --> 00:00:51.240
a list the P K I owner supplies, and
it warns inside a ninety-day window.
